WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.160
After two "G.I. Joe" films that&nbsp;
failed to set the world on fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:09.760
Paramount is taking the origin story approach with&nbsp;
"Snake Eyes." But with a new cast and fresh story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:14.640
comes new details to account for. Here are the&nbsp;
biggest unanswered questions from "Snake Eyes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:16.880
G.I. Joe Origins."

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:22.000
Throughout most of the history of "G.I. Joe," the&nbsp;
black bodysuit-clad ninja commando Snake Eyes is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:27.840
rarely unmasked and doesn't speak — and actor Ray&nbsp;
Park plays him this way in "The Rise of Cobra"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.960
and "Retaliation." After all, giving Snake Eyes&nbsp;
a voice and unmasking him in the films would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:37.520
have gone against everything fans knew about&nbsp;
the character from his previous appearances.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:43.280
In the comic book "G.I. Joe: A Real American Hero"&nbsp;
#27, we learn in the "Snake Eyes: The Origin"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.480
story that Snake Eyes' face and vocal cords were&nbsp;
severely burned in a helicopter explosion while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.960
the commando was serving in one of his first&nbsp;
missions with the Joes. However, in "Snake Eyes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.520
G.I. Joe Origins," we learn that Snake Eyes&nbsp;
suffered a traumatic event in his childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:02.720
growing up into a drifter who seeks retribution&nbsp;
for the tragedy. The reason for his new appearance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:07.200
is simple: We're meeting Snake Eyes earlier&nbsp;
in life, and he doesn't actually put on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.120
helmet and face shield associated with&nbsp;
the character until the final scene.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.560
"No one cared who I was until I put on the mask."

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:19.840
Naturally, the film leaves the door open for more&nbsp;
Snake Eyes and "G.I. Joe Origins" film adventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.880
so only time will tell whether Henry&nbsp;
Golding's iteration of the character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.040
will get to the point where Snake Eyes&nbsp;
doesn't remove his mask and ceases to speak.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.280
That scenario appears to be unlikely for&nbsp;
Paramount and Hasbro in the short term,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.880
since it would make no sense for them to&nbsp;
conceal Golding, whose career has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:39.840
on the rise since his breakthrough in the 2018&nbsp;
hit romantic comedy drama "Crazy Rich Asians."

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.200
Making a memorable first impression&nbsp;
in "Snake Eyes" is Haruka Abe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.080
who plays the Arashikage Clan's head of security&nbsp;
— a new character in the "G.I. Joe" franchise.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.400
The exciting thing for Abe is, Akiko is&nbsp;
far from just a functional character in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:58.480
"Snake Eyes," as director Robert Schwentke&nbsp;
gave the actor just as many action scenes as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.720
her co-stars. Her character is so pivotal,&nbsp;
in fact, that she's getting a "Snake Eyes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.000
G.I. Joe Origins" action figure produced&nbsp;
by Hasbro. That's a true honor, since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.880
action figures are as pivotal to the success of&nbsp;
the franchise as all its other forms of media.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:18.000
On top of all that, Akiko's storyline is&nbsp;
primed to continue — Akiko provides Snake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.760
Eyes with his signature costume and&nbsp;
mask and joins him in his quest "to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.640
get Tommy back" after Tommy swears off the&nbsp;
Arashikage Clan and becomes Storm Shadow.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.160
Mulling Akiko's potential involvement&nbsp;
in future "G.I. Joe" installments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.640
Abe is certainly up for more Akiko,&nbsp;
telling "Looper" in an exclusive interview,

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:39.440
"I think there's so much to be explored about&nbsp;
her background and also her relationship, her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:44.800
dynamic with Storm Shadow and Snake Eyes. So yeah,&nbsp;
I can't wait to see where her character will go."

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.560
Given that four major "G.I. Joe" characters&nbsp;
have been recast for "Snake Eyes," it appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:56.160
the franchise is intent on starting from scratch.&nbsp;
Since the first two "G.I. Joe" films fell short of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:01.920
box office blockbuster status, the franchise had&nbsp;
to do some major retooling, and a reboot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.720
movie series was the most sensible way to do it.
While future installments of "G.I. Joe Origins"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.760
will depend on box office performance and fan&nbsp;
reception,the ending of "Snake Eyes" promises a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.360
return of Snake Eyes, Storm Shadow, the Baroness,&nbsp;
and Scarlett. That could come in the form of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.640
"Snake Eyes 2," but more likely, if the studio&nbsp;
is serious about the backstory concept, they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.840
could return in a different "G.I. Joe: Origins"&nbsp;
movie featuring another Joe or Cobra character.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.880
As for the possibility of seeing any of the actors&nbsp;
from "The Rise of Cobra" or "Retaliation" turn up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.280
it's pretty unlikely.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.720
While the ending of "Snake Eyes" promises&nbsp;
more adventures with the new cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:42.080
what those adventures will&nbsp;
be and who they will involve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.640
remains a mystery. Based on the final act&nbsp;
in "Snake Eyes," one of the angles will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:50.800
involve Snake Eyes and Storm Shadow, and&nbsp;
to a larger extent, the Joes and Cobra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:54.960
since the Baroness appears to have recruited&nbsp;
Tommy into the ranks of the organization.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.920
Since "G.I. Joe Origins" is part of the "Snake&nbsp;
Eyes" film title, it's reasonable to think that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.160
more origin movies could be on the way.&nbsp;
Whatever their current plans might be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:09.200
Paramount Pictures isn't tipping its hand in terms&nbsp;
of the new direction of the franchise just yet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.320
However, "Deadline" reported in May 2021 that&nbsp;
screenwriters Joe Shrapnel and Anna Waterhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.640
who co-wrote the 2019 biographical thriller&nbsp;
"Seberg," starring Kristen Stewart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.520
are writing their own movie&nbsp;
set in the "G.I. Joe" universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:26.240
meant to serve as a sequel to and build off&nbsp;
of what was established in "Snake Eyes."

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.800
Apart from any potential new "G.I. Joe" films,&nbsp;
at least one other beloved character from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.360
franchise is getting their own spinoff.&nbsp;
In February 2021, "Deadline" reported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:40.160
that streaming giant Amazon was developing a&nbsp;
standalone Lady Jaye series based on the Joes'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:45.280
famed undercover operative. Making her debut&nbsp;
in the "G.I. Joe" animated series in 1984,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.760
Lady Jaye was first played in live action by&nbsp;
Adrianne Palicki in "G.I. Joe: Retaliation."

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:50.960
According to "Deadline,"

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.160
"The series will be a standalone&nbsp;
story centered around Jaye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.440
which will also connect to the&nbsp;
larger 'G.I. Joe' universe."

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.600
Could that mean that we could see Golding and&nbsp;
his fellow "Snake Eyes" actors appear in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:06.720
"Lady Jaye" spinoff? While no actors or story&nbsp;
timeline have been revealed yet, it's possible.

